    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-36521: differentiating f_xx with respect to y gives 2 at (1,0,1), and differentiating f_xz with respect to z gives 12, totaling 14. q-65132: continuous mixed partials cancel, leaving f_xx(0,3)=6-3=3. q-129446: the slopes are (0,-3/4), giving z+2=-(3/4)(y-4). q-129444: the slopes are (-1,3), giving z-2=-(x+1)+3(y-1). q-37604: the gradient is (e,e,-e), giving w-e=e(x-1)+e(y-1)-e(z-1). q-129485: the gradient is (pi,-2,-2), giving w+pi=pi(x+1)-2(y-1)-2(z-1). These tangent equations rearrange to the selected forms. q-73860: horizontal tangent planes require 3x^2-3=0 and 2y+2=0; substituting gives (-1,-1,1) and (1,-1,-3). q-37982: the normal (3y,3x-1/y,-1) must be parallel to (3,5,-1); the last coordinates fix the proportionality, giving y=1, x=2, z=6. The four numerical linear approximations are q-98328: 4+4(-0.05)-2(0.04)=3.72; q-129631: 0+0(0.01)+2(0.02)=0.04; q-98340: 6-4(0.04)-0.01+3(0.02)=5.89; q-129659: 12+4(-0.03)+12(0.1)+36(0.04)=14.52. q-129748: the base value 1 and gradient (1,-1,-1) give 1+(x-1)-(y+1)-(z+1)=-2+x-y-z. q-98554: the base value 0 and gradient (1,1,-1/e) give (x-1)+(y-1)-(z-e)/e=-1+x+y-z/e. q-160406: the determinant is e^(u+v)(2v)-e^(u+v)(2u)=2e^(u+v)(v-u). q-81264: the determinant is (2u)(2v)-(-2v)(2u)=8uv. No prior submitted answers or grades were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
